-- title:
--   Supersingular chart at q=3: DVR, Drinfeld chart, nodes, inertia
-- statement:
--   **Ambient data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ be an integer with $q\nmid M'$, and fix a guard prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\kappa$-field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated over $\kappa$ by the expansions of $j$ and of $j(M'\tau)$; the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, of those places $w$ which are rational (the map $\kappa\to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w(j)$ on the generator `jGeomGen` lies in the set `ssJSet q κ` of supersingular $j$-invariants in characteristic $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`: the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change (adjoin the coefficientwise images) of the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions $j(d\tau)$, $d\mid M'$, sits inside the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants and compatible with residues of constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and, for elements of non-zero residue, divisor orders (the remaining clauses of the structure are summarised here). The hypothesis `hR₀` is the compatibility with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a $\kappa$-Laurent series, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo $\mathfrak m_A$. Finally $s\in W$ is a distinguished supersingular place.
--
--   **Small constant field.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A\cap k_0$ (the preimage of $A$ in $k_0$) is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is a henselian local ring, and that its residue field is algebraically closed; `hκ` states that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to some element of $k_0\cap A$, i.e. $A=(A\cap k_0)+\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and tame uniformiser.** $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (so $K_b=k_0$), $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ with $x\in A_b\iff x\in A$, and $\varpi_b\ne 0$ is an element of $A_b$ generating $\mathfrak m_{A_b}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Equip `fieldBar q M'` with the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ whose elements are exactly those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients (at every index $n\in\mathbb Z$) lie in $k_0$. Then there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (i) $W_0\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$: for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (ii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$.
--
--   (iii) *Specialisation at $s$.* For every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-image lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $g$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference (image of $g$) $-\,c$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$.
--
--   (iv) *Level stability.* For every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f$ with $f\in F_0$ and `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f ∈ F₀`: $f\in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$. Here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` characterised by `IsLevelAutBar` (the $q$-expansion identity for the $\gamma$-translate relative to a complex embedding sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$), and the identity if no such automorphism exists.
--
--   (v) *Affine chart.* There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that: the structure map $A_b\to B$ is the inclusion $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $k_0(\text{image of }K_b)$ and $F_0$, and conversely every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_bB$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element; and $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at it, i.e. for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in W_0$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$. Moreover the image of $j$ (the inclusion of the base change of `jq`) lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   (vi) *Pole witness.* There is an element $b$ of $F_0$ lying in $B$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ satisfying: $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$; and $j\in V$ with $p(j)\notin\mathfrak m_V$ for every monic $p\in k_0[X]$ whose coefficients lie in $A$.
--
--   (vii) *Separation of the other supersingular places.* For every $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$ there is an element $b$ of $F_0$ lying in $B$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$ which satisfies the specialisation property (iii) at $s'$ (with $V$ in place of $W_0$).
--
--   (viii) *Drinfeld model of the reduction.* For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the Drinfeld function field, of the automorphisms attached to $C_s$) such that: $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, where `placeWidthChar` is `jWidthChar q (s(j))` divided by the $j$-ramification of $s$, and `jWidthChar 3 j` equals $6$ for $j=0$ and $1$ otherwise; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; on constants, $\rho$ agrees with the residue map $A_b\to\kappa$ followed by $\kappa\to$ `quotField`; every element of `quotField` is $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $\rho(h)\ne 0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements of `quotField` which lie in the image of `CoordRing q κ` in the Drinfeld function field; and $\rho$ is equivariant for the level automorphisms in the sense that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\overline\gamma,1)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\gamma,\alpha)\mapsto\det\gamma\cdot\alpha^{q+1}$) and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f ∈ B`, the image under $\rho$ of the latter equals `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\overline\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   (ix) *Drinfeld model with inertia, uniform in $\zeta$.* For every ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbb F_{q^2}\to\kappa$, taken as the algebra structure, and every proof that `CoordRing q κ` is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ with $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` there is $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with the same five properties as in (viii) (kernel the ideal of the image of $\varpi_b$, compatibility on constants, fraction-field property, description of the image, $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance), and in addition: there is $\eta\in\{1,q\}$ such that for every $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$, every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` which maps $k_0$ into itself, every $\alpha\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $\iota(\alpha)=$ `A.tameCharacter π τ` (the residue of $\tau\pi/\pi$), and every semilinear automorphism $g$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) (the coefficientwise action of $\tau$): the subring $B$ is $g$-stable, and for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ is $\alpha^{q+1}$, whenever $(\mathrm{diag}(1,d^{\eta})^{-1},\alpha^{\eta})$ lies in `hSubgroup q` and $f\in B$ has $g\cdot f\in B$, one has $\rho(g\cdot f)=$ `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\mathrm{diag}(1,d^{\eta})^{-1},\alpha^{\eta})$ applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   (x) *Nodes.* There exist: a proof that the base change of $j$ lies in `R₀.integers`; a proof that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a proof `hJK` that the expansion [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) of $j(q\tau)$ lies in `fieldBar q M'`; an element $a_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q}=$ the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$ (the Hasse relation); and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, such that:
--
--   (x.1) `nodes` has exactly $q+1$ elements;
--
--   (x.2) there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ of the form `Subring.closure` of the set of images of elements of $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T\subseteq F_0$, such that every $O\in$ `nodes` contains $B_c$ and is the localisation of $B_c$ in $O$: $f\in O$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$;
--
--   (x.3) the level automorphisms permute the nodes: for every $\zeta$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O\in$ `nodes` there is $O'\in$ `nodes` with $f\in O\iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$ (for $f$ with both memberships in $F_0$); and the action is transitive: for every $\zeta$ and all $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ realising $f\in O\iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$;
--
--   (x.4) distinct nodes are distinguished: for $O\ne O'$ in `nodes` there is $f$ in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   (x.5) dichotomy for valuation subrings: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$ which satisfies the specialisation property (iii) at $s$ with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains $B$ (every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$) or dominates a node: there is $O\in$ `nodes` with $O\subseteq V$ such that every non-unit of $O$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$;
--
--   (x.6) and for every $O\in$ `nodes`: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; $O\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$; every $f\in O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0\cap A$ by a non-unit of $O$. Moreover there exists $E_0\ge 1$ together with: a unit $v$ of $A\cap k_0$ (i.e. $v,v^{-1}\in A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\,v$; a proof that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$; elements $c_x,c_y\in O$; a unit $u$ of $O$; a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the completion of $O$ at $\mathfrak m_O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the completion $\widehat{A\cap k_0}$ at the parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is $\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$; and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that: $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the images of constants $x\in k_0\cap A$ to the corresponding constants of the crossing model; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$, while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0$, is not in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$; the element $j(q\tau)-a_0$ (the class of `jqNModC` minus the constant $a_0$) lies in $F_0$ and in $O$, and $\iota$ sends it to $w_V\cdot V^{e}$ for some unit $w_V$ of the crossing model and some $e\ge 1$.
--
--   Furthermore, for each such $O$ there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with: $O\subseteq W_x$; $W_x\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$; $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; an element $t\in W_x$ such that for every $p\in k_0[X]$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; $c_x\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y$ a unit at $W_x$ (whenever these lie in $W_x$); and the following specialisation law: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers` and which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ has non-negative order, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ precisely when the $R_0$-residue of $g$ vanishes, and if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $g$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that residue, the difference of the two images is a non-unit of $O$; finally $W_x$ separates $O$ from the other nodes: for every $O'\in$ `nodes` with $O'\ne O$ there is $f\in O'$ with $f\notin W_x$.
--
--   Finally, for each such $O$ there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with: $B_x\subseteq B\cap O$; every $f\in B_x$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ has non-negative order; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$, i.e. $f\in O$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$; every $f\in F_0$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$, $h\ne 0$; $B_x$ is the subring generated by the images of $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T\subseteq F_0$; and there is $b\in B_x$ with the following pole property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$, with the image of $\pi_0$ in $\mathfrak m_V$, with $j\in V$ such that $p(j)\notin\mathfrak m_V$ for every monic $p\in k_0[X]$ with coefficients in $A$, and such that some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$, one has $b\notin V$.
--
--   This is the case $q=3$, at a rigid auxiliary level controlled by the guard prime $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the package describing the semistable local structure of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular point: a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ of the level field $F_0$ above the supersingular place $s$, an affine chart $B$ whose reduction modulo $\varpi_b$ is the Drinfeld (Igusa) curve together with its $\Gamma_0(M')$- and tame-inertia equivariance (the inertia clause carrying an exponent $\eta\in\{1,q\}$), and the $q+1$ node local rings with their crossing models $UV=\pi_0^{E_0}$, separated on distinct components. It feeds the downstream statements that assemble smooth-point packages, node presentations and node charts with the Hasse relation on $j$ and the Drinfeld inertia action at $q=3$.
